 diagram above shows the vector $\\mathbf{a}$. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $-\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{a}$?"] [17592186097042 "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $3$, while the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $4$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186097045 "The vector $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ has magnitude $7$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overrightarrow{AB}$?"] [17592186097247 "If a curve $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by $y = 2e^{x}(x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = 0$."] [17592186097260 "If a curve $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by $y = 8x^{3}\\sin x$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x = \\frac{π}{2}$."] [17592186106040 "The closed, positively oriented curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector on $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$"] [17592186106041 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=7\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+24\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $b(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106043 "The closed curve $C$ is defined as $\\mathbf{r}(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+8\\operatorname{cos}t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$ The outward-pointing unit normal vector for $C$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\frac{a(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+b(t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}}{||{\\mathbf{r}}^{'}(t)||}.\n$$\n\nFind the function $a(t).$\n\n*Hint: Observe that $C$ is traversed clockwise.*"] [17592186106060 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2xy,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106063 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=-3xz,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=\\sqrt{2}x+\\sqrt{2}y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$${∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?"] [17592186106094 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=⟨k,1,1⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨5,0,4⟩$, and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨6,2,5⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106095 "Find $t$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{p}=⟨3,t,t⟩$, $\\mathbf{q}=⟨1,3,1⟩$, and $\\mathbf{r}=⟨1,1,3⟩$ are coplanar."] [17592186106098 "Let $\\mathbf{p}=⟨\\sqrt{2},1,-1⟩$ and $\\mathbf{q}=⟨\\sqrt{8},-\\sqrt{3},1⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{p}$ onto $\\mathbf{q}.$"] [17592186106120 "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=⟨1,3,2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{b}=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$"] [17592186106121 "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-2,-3,-1⟩$ and $b = ⟨1, 2, 1⟩$."] [17592186106126 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=⟨3,1,-3⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨2,6,-2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨0,1,-4⟩$. Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$."] [17592186106127 "Let $\\mathbf{p}=⟨2,-1,0⟩$, $\\mathbf{q}=⟨3,-3,2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{r}=⟨1,-4,1⟩.$ Find $\\mathbf{r}\\cdot (\\mathbf{q}\\times \\mathbf{p}).$"] [17592186106128 "Find $\\mathbf{b}\\cdot (\\mathbf{c}\\times \\mathbf{a})$, if $-\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (3\\mathbf{b}\\times (-2\\mathbf{c}))=24.$"] [17592186106129 "Find $\\mathbf{c}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{a})$, if $\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c}=⟨2,3,0⟩$ and $\\mathbf{a}=⟨1,-2,2⟩.$"] [17592186106130 "Find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$ given that $\\mathbf{a}=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c}=⟨-2,1,8⟩.$"] [17592186106131 "Given that $\\mathbf{a}=⟨0,-2,3⟩,$ $\\mathbf{b}=⟨4,-2,1⟩,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨3,-1,2⟩,$ find $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}\\times \\mathbf{c})$ using the definition of the scalar triple product."] [17592186106213 "Let $\\mathbf{p}=⟨-1,1,2⟩$ and $\\mathbf{q}=⟨4,x,1⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{p}$ onto $\\mathbf{q}$ is zero, find the value of $x.$"] [17592186106214 "Let $\\mathbf{p}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{q}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Given that the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{p}$ onto $\\mathbf{q}$ is $0,$ find the value of $x.$"] [17592186106309 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{x}=⟨3,5,0⟩$, $\\mathbf{y}=⟨3,2,0⟩$ and $\\mathbf{z}=⟨3,4,5⟩.$"] [17592186106310 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=⟨-3,0,-2⟩$, $\\mathbf{b}=⟨1,5,-3⟩$, and $\\mathbf{c}=⟨2,-1,4⟩$."] [17592186106478 "Suppose $|\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{c}\\hspace{0.167em}|=18$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{d}$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{c}$ onto $\\mathbf{d}.$"] [17592186114970 "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-\\left(\\frac{1}{t-2}\\right)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\operatorname{cos}2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =(4t-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{3t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+\\operatorname{cos}2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114973 "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{2}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{t}\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115760 "Find $(u(t)\\mathbf{f}(t))^{'}$ where $\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}t \\\\ 2t-8 \\\\ {5}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$"] [17592186115762 "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\cdot \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =20t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-2t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+(2+5t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & ={t}^{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+({t}^{2}+t)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115764 "Find $(\\mathbf{f}\\times \\mathbf{g})^{'}(t)$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3{t}^{2} \\\\ t+4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\hspace{2em}\\mathbf{g}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ -2{t}^{2} \\\\ 5t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [17592186115767 "If $\\mathbf{f}(u)=\\begin{bmatrix}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(\\mathbf{f}∘u)^{'}(t)=$"] [17592186115768 "Find $(u(t)\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}$ where $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨3{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}3-t,\\hspace{0.222em}3t⟩$ and $u(t) = t^{3}$."] [17592186115772 "If $\\mathbf{f}(t)=\\operatorname{cos}u\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(1-{u}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+12\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k}$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}$ then $(\\mathbf{f}∘u)^{'}(t)=$"] [17592186115775 "Differentiate $\\mathbf{f}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{f}(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\hspace{0.222em}6-t,\\hspace{0.222em}7t⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}1-{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186115776 "Find the value of $(3\\mathbf{h}(t)-2\\mathbf{g}(t))^{'}$ at $t = 2$, if\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{h}(t) & =⟨2{t}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}t-3,\\hspace{0.222em}8+{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{g}(t) & =⟨{t}^{2}+2t,\\hspace{0.222em}8,\\hspace{0.222em}2{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186120071 "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}u,\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}4v\\operatorname{cos}u⟩.$"] [17592186120073 "$${∬}_{D}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi \\}$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u\\operatorname{cos}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?"] [17592186120079 "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨-u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}3v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 4.$"] [17592186120091 "$${∬}_{D}\\boxed{\\phantom{AAAAAAAA}}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u-{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?"] [17592186120272 "![](images/d1/d162245ac19c3ef9ae63d602fb4e188ddfd241a1a604304f6c272c3902ce1e93.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}2t,\\hspace{0.222em}\\operatorname{cos}3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$"] [17592186120274 "![](images/c7/c76cff47179efaaf490430856b8db1f2b85f0d2000d34725a9c40a9e150ccf6b.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{r}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}t,\\hspace{0.222em}2t,\\hspace{0.222em}{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom $t = 1$ to $t = e$."] [17592186120275 "Find the arc length of the curve $$\n\\mathbf{f}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}t+t\\operatorname{sin}t,\\hspace{0.222em}\\operatorname{sin}t-t\\operatorname{cos}t,\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩\n$$\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=3.$"] [17592186120281 "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{f}(t)={e}^{t}(\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k})$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$"] [17592186120527 "![](images/b6/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\hspace{0.222em}3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=2?$"] [17592186120528 "![](images/9b/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf{g}(t)=⟨2{t}^{3/2},\\hspace{0.222em}3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=3.$"] [17592186124251 "Find the gradient of the product $f(x,y) g(x,y)$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =xy,\\hspace{1em} &  & \\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=y\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+x\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}, &  &  \\\\ g(x,y) & =\\sqrt{xy},\\hspace{1em} &  & \\mathrm{∇}g(x,y)=\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2x}\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\sqrt{xy}}{2y}\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186124938 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n\\lim_{\\mathbf{x}\\to (0,0)}\\frac{xy-x{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2xy}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [17592186124943 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $\\mathrm{∇}f=\\mathbf{F},$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=-y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(3-x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186124944 "Given that $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-x$, find the points $(x,y)$ where $\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=\\mathbf{0}.$"] [17592186124954 "Find the gradient of the product $g(x,y)h(x,y),$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x,y) & =3{x}^{2}-4y,\\hspace{2em} &  & \\mathrm{∇}g(x,y)=6x\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}-4\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}, &  &  \\\\ h(x,y) & =2{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\hspace{2em} &  & \\mathrm{∇}h(x,y)=4x{y}^{2}\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+4{x}^{2}y\\text{ }\\mathbf{j}. &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186124955 "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{-t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$"] [17592186124956 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]$ at $t=1$ given that\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+3y}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\n$$\nand\n$\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{t}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186124959 "If $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+xz$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=t\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{t}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}+e\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{k},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$"]}
